<stringmatch name="x64syscall #3: on, kernel_call recovers the number and all three arguments, and returns the syscall's own result" min="1" max="1">return syscall\(a[0-9]+,a[0-9]+,a[0-9]+,a[0-9]+\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="x64syscall #4: on, split_setup keeps RAX alone -- its RDI is set two blocks back, which the in-block walk does not claim" min="1" max="1">return syscall\(v[0-9]+\);</stringmatch>
